1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,940
大家都有酒了吗 我要开始感恩节祝酒了
Does everyone have a glass? I'm just giving my Thanksgiving toast.

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:05,661
拜托老爸 你不觉得这样很怪吗
Oh, come on, Dad. Isn't it weird that

3
00:00:05,661 --> 00:00:07,500
每年都要选一个不知为何
every year you single out one person

4
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,729
反正就是让你觉得格外骄傲的人
who somehow made you extra proud this year?

5
00:00:10,729 --> 00:00:12,000
这让我们其他人觉得...
It makes the rest of us feel like we --

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:12,540
是你 克莱尔
It's you, Claire.

7
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:14,240
真棒 我就知道
Yeah! I knew it!

8
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:16,160
还有你 菲尔 米奇尔
And you, Phil, and you, Mitchell.

9
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:17,360
实际上是你们所有人
Actually, it's all of you.

10
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:19,100
我知道我在家庭中引发竞争
I know I get a hard time

11
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,100
你们都对我都颇有微词
for stirring up competition in the family,

12
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:22,554
但瞧瞧结果
but look at the results.

13
00:00:22,554 --> 00:00:25,260
菲尔新开了家魔术用品店
Phil scoring with his new magic shop.

14
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:26,560
小卡带的球队赢得了重要比赛
Cam winning the big game.

15
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:28,020
克莱尔赢了跑步比赛
Claire winning the race.

16
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:29,980
而米奇尔吓跑了那个小偷
And Mitchell scaring away that burglar.

17
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:32,640
你也是赢家 杰
And you are a winner, too, Jay.

18
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:35,020
他想跟乔共度更多时光
He wanted to spend more time with Joe,

19
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:36,720
所以他每天
so he's dropping him off

20
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:39,040
都送他上学 接他放学
and picking him up from school every day.

21
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:40,180
爸爸 她怎么了
Dad, what is wrong with her?

22
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:41,480
我挑战她
I challenged her to get

23
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:43,420
一周内走十万步
to 100,000 steps in a week.

24
00:00:43,545 --> 00:00:44,800
-那很容易 -真容易
- That's easy. - That's so easy.

25
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:45,698
不算购物
Without shopping.

26
00:00:45,698 --> 00:00:47,243
-我明白挑战难处了 -不
- I get -- I get the challenge. - No.

27
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,860
她还剩1000步就获得荣誉了
She's 1,000 steps from glory.

28
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:50,900
跟你们一样
Like the rest of you,

29
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:52,680
她的动力来源于我的吝于赞美
she was motivated by my stingy praise.

30
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:55,140
我环顾四周 看到的全是赢家
As I look around the room, I see nothing but winners,

31
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:56,540
我感到十分骄傲
and I couldn't be prouder.

32
00:00:56,540 --> 00:00:57,380
敬我们
To us!

33
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:00,040
这里的每个人都是赢家
Everyone here is a winner.

34
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:19,141
你知道这场重要比赛让我很紧张
You knew I was nervous about the big game,

35
00:01:19,141 --> 00:01:20,480
所以你拿出了我的 好吧
so you set out my -- Okay.

36
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,000
糖屑是给英雄准备的
Sprinkles are for heroes.

37
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:23,300
给 二爸
Here, Daddy.

38
00:01:23,420 --> 00:01:24,960
谢谢你保护我们
Thank you for protecting us.

39
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:29,040
我们都为米奇尔那天做的事感到骄傲
We're all so proud of Mitchell about what happened the other day.

40
00:01:30,054 --> 00:01:31,349
我的想法是我们可以...
What I was thinking was, we could...

41
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:32,460
天啊
Oh, my gosh!

42
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:33,660
有人闯入了吗
Was there a break-in?

43
00:01:33,723 --> 00:01:35,500
对啊对啊 简直要疯了
Yeah, yeah. It was -- It was crazy.

44
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,060
我当时就冲他吼叫
I just started yelling at him,

45
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:38,720
我好像就把他吓跑了 所以...
and I guess I scared him away, so...

46
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:41,440
天啊 亲爱的 你没事吧
Oh, my gosh, sweetie. Are you okay?

47
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,760
是的 我没事
Yeah, yeah, I'm fine. I'm fine.

48
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,300
-你真勇敢 -宝贝
- You're so brave. - Oh, honey.

49
00:01:44,860 --> 00:01:45,620
万分骄傲
So proud.

50
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:48,560
如果小偷回来了 而勇敢二爸不在的话
If the robber comes back when Brave Daddy isn't here,

51
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:50,480
-我们可以用这个 -不不
- we can use these. - Okay, no, no, no, no.

52
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:52,660
那是我在学校没收的
I had to confiscate those at school.

53
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:53,577
这很危险
They're very dangerous,

54
00:01:53,577 --> 00:01:56,320
而且你最好避开这种亚洲人刻板印象物件
and, plus, you should avoid the cliche.

55
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:59,000
没收违禁品是我在学校新工作的一部分
Confiscating contraband is part of my new job at school.

56
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:00,920
我最近升职为
I was recently promoted to

57
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:02,940
代理[演戏]副校长了
acting vice principal.

58
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:04,320
这跟演戏毫无关系
Which has nothing to do with acting.

59
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,120
他们非常明确地跟我说了
That was made very clear to me.

60
00:02:06,749 --> 00:02:08,913
你看起来有些紧张
Hey. Hey. Y-You seem a little nervous.

61
00:02:08,913 --> 00:02:10,480
你是在担心这场重要比赛吗
Are you -- Are you worried about the big game?

62
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:11,840
是啊 我有些紧张
Yeah. I'm a little nervous.

63
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:13,720
响尾蛇队过去六年里都打败了我们
The Rattlesnakes have beat us the last six years,

64
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:14,900
而我们不能输
and we cannot lose.

65
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,157
你这么紧张是因为他们的教练是女人吗
Is any of this because their coach is a woman?

66
00:02:17,157 --> 00:02:19,500
我们不该支持她吗 因为
I mean, shouldn't we be rooting for her, because --

67
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:22,220
因为她是一个执教橄榄球的异性恋吗
Oh, what, because she's another straight person coaching football?

68
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:24,479
-祝你好运 -谢谢你 亲爱的
- Well, good luck. - Thank you, sweetie.

69
00:02:24,479 --> 00:02:26,380
我无法保证我让你感受到的骄傲
You know, I can't promise that I'll make you as proud as your daddy

70
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:28,760
和打跑了小偷的二爸一样多 但我会努力
who fought off a burglar, but I will try.

71
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,740
有传言说后援俱乐部
You know, there's murmurs that the booster club

72
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:33,060
要把给我们的一些经费转给科学项目
is gonna divert some of our money to the science program.

73
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:35,500
因为霸气的肯尼迪家族就是这么变酷的
Because that's what made the Kennedys cool, you know --

74
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:36,980
靠在草坪上玩科学什么的
playing science on the lawn.

75
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:41,180
第一个想出怎么把号码布一次贴到位的人
Ow! The first person who figures out how to stick these numbers

76
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:43,120
肯定能发大财
right on is gonna be rich.

77
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:45,300
你可以在穿上背心之前先贴好啊
You could just pin it to your shirt before you put it on.

78
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:48,020
你跟别人分享过这个点子吗
Have you shared this idea with anyone else?

79
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:51,120
艾丽克斯小时候 我会把她放进慢跑婴儿车里
When Alex was a baby, I used to throw her in a jogging stroller,

80
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,480
她是我的跑步伙伴
and she was my running buddy.

81
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:55,660
这周她得知我要跑一万米时
This week, when she found out I was doing a 10K,

82
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,580
就坚持要来
she insisted on coming.

83
00:02:58,020 --> 00:02:58,420
无聊死了
Snore.

84
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:01,220
我把我妈当做我的白痴心理学论文的对象
I'm using my mom as a subject for my stupid psych paper

85
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:03,060
因为我开始太晚 没法领猴子研究
because I started too late to sign out a monkey.

86
00:03:03,460 --> 00:03:05,540
论文是关于积极与消极强化的
It's about positive versus negative reinforcement.

87
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:08,240
比赛前半程我会喊 "你能做到的 妈"
First half of the race -- "You can do it, Mom!"

88
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:10,340
后半程则是 "算了吧 女人"
Second half -- "It's not your day, lady!"

89
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:12,060
幸好 做完实验后
Thankfully, after it's done,

90
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:13,520
给猴子买的香蕉可以给她补充能量
I'll still be able to give out the banana I bought.

91
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:16,040
多谢你照顾乔
Thank you so much for taking care of Joe.

92
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:18,540
我还得去店里买点晚餐食材
I still have to get some things from the store for dinner.

93
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:19,660
没问题
It's no problem.

94
00:03:19,660 --> 00:03:21,976
我有很多知识可以传授
I got a lot of knowledge to pass on.

95
00:03:21,976 --> 00:03:24,385
你有在持续练习打嗝吗
You been practicing your burping drills?

96
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:25,280
是的
Yes!

97
00:03:25,290 --> 00:03:27,286
-好些了 -好 闲聊完了
- Better. - Okay, enough chitchat.

98
00:03:27,286 --> 00:03:29,536
给我促销的VIP票
Give me the V.I.P. Pass for the sale.

99
00:03:29,559 --> 00:03:31,960
大家都听说过H.布朗夫曼服装的
Everybody's heard of the H. Bronfman Clothiers

100
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:33,640
黑五促销 那时候大伙儿
Black Friday sale where the hoi polloi

101
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:35,320
像动物一样疯狂争抢晚礼服
fight over tuxedos like animals.

102
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:37,360
但是在感恩节
But on Thanksgiving Day,

103
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:39,620
极少数人会受邀当第一批进场的买家
a select few are invited to get first crack.

104
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,360
如果我能把要的都买齐
If I get everything I want,

105
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:44,700
我的燕尾服就会在小姑娘房里脱到只剩两成
that tux will be 80% off in Tammy Bosworth's dorm room.

106
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:46,040
黑金卡
Black gold.

107
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,872
这是俱乐部成员当做小费给我的
I got it as a tip from some club members

108
00:03:47,872 --> 00:03:49,780
他让我弄来几瓶灰雁伏特加
who had me "deal" with some geese.

109
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:52,160
你休想玷污这次体验
You will not taint this experience.

110
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,620
克莱尔 你为什么贴着号码布
Claire, why do you have that number?

111
00:03:55,644 --> 00:03:57,540
你参加选美比赛了吗
Are you in a pageant?

112
00:03:57,540 --> 00:04:00,580
她要跑一万米 她的表现一定会很棒
She's running a 10K. And she is going to do great.

113
00:04:00,883 --> 00:04:05,720
我就知道你会让我们感到骄傲
I know that you're gonna make us oh-so proud!

114
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,330
显然这本该是群抱
Obviously, this was meant to be a group hug,

115
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:09,520
而我的邀请函在邮寄时遗失了
and my invitation got lost in the mail. Mm.

116
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,760
菲尔 你为了变魔术
Phil... that crazy phone booth

117
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:13,360
订的那个疯狂电话亭
that you ordered for your magic trick --

118
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:14,774
已经在我家了
It's already at my house.

119
00:04:14,774 --> 00:04:16,503
提前两天到了吗
It's here two days early?!

120
00:04:16,503 --> 00:04:19,753
我今天就能拍摄教程
I can shoot my how-to video today!

121
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:20,960
海莉 好戏上演了
Haley! Showtime!

122
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:22,900
毫无疑问 二战中
It goes without saying that the greatest trick

123
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:25,380
最伟大的魔术就是诺曼底电话亭
to come out of World War II is the Normandy Phone Booth.

124
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:29,500
多年来 它的名声时起时落
Over the years, its reputation has ebbed and flowed.

125
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:30,480
众所周知 在1969年的
It was famously booed

126
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:32,680
纳拉干塞特魔术节上它遭到了大家的喝倒彩
at the 1969 Narragansett Magic Festival.

127
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,500
当然 那时候
Of course, this is a time

128
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:36,360
大部分人都在抗议魔术
when most people are into protest magic.

129
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:40,700
所以很自然 他们会对经典魔术嗤之以鼻
So naturally, they would thumb their nose at a classic trick

130
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:44,180
那就是一个英勇的士兵冲进电话亭
where a heroic soldier dashes into a phone booth

131
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:46,320
打了拯救世界的电话
to make a world-saving call

132
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:48,480
而电话亭慢慢灌满了水
while it slowly fills with water!

133
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:50,220
这多赞啊 嬉皮士们
Come on, hippies!

134
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:51,880
天啊
God!

135
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:55,660
小家伙 你出去玩吧
All right, buddy. Run outside and play real quick.

136
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:56,800
我要去楼上忙些事
I'm gonna take care of something upstairs.

137
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,100
我得更新我在
I had to update my profile pic

138
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,660
一款新社交媒体软件"内缝线"上的用户照片
on this new social-media app called Inseam.

139
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:04,280
这软件超酷的 基本还没人知道
It's super cool. No one knows about it.

140
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:06,858
有些老家伙用它分享自制成衣
Some old guys were using it for home tailoring,

141
00:05:06,858 --> 00:05:08,340
但之后两个布鲁克林DJ
but then two Brooklyn deejays

142
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:10,600
开始在上面分享一些视频 然后就火了
started sharing a couple of videos on it, and it blew up.

143
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:11,780
太严肃了
Not approachable.

144
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:13,000
太亲和了
Too approachable.

145
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,640
完美
There's my guy.

146
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:17,960
怎么了
What's up?

147
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:19,280
伙计 我刚准备离开
Dude, I was just about to leave,

148
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:20,855
结果在内缝线上看见了你的新照片
and I saw your new pic popped up on Inseam.

149
00:05:20,855 --> 00:05:22,160
你也用内缝线吗
You're on Inseam?

150
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,320
是的 我已经用了一周了
Yes, I've been on it for a week.

151
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:26,360
你看看照片 乔在你身后的树上
Okay, look at your picture. Joe is in a tree behind you.

152
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:31,100
天啊 他就在那里
Oh, my God, he's right there!

153
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:32,300
等等 乔
Hang on, Joe!

154
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:32,960
喂
Hello?

155
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:34,628
乔怎么了
What's going on with Joe?

156
00:05:34,628 --> 00:05:35,888
你也用内缝线吗
You're on Inseam?

157
00:05:35,888 --> 00:05:37,160
当然了
Of course I'm on Inseam.

158
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,880
我儿子挂在树上了吗
Is my son hanging from a tree?

159
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:41,139
真棒 你信了
Oh, that's great! You fell for it.

160
00:05:41,139 --> 00:05:43,000
我的改图技术越来越出神入化啊
I'm, uh -- I'm getting pretty good at Photoshop.

161
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,080
那是假照片吗
That's a fake picture?

162
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:46,580
是啊 我有许多张乔做危险事情的照片
Yeah, I got a bunch of Joe doing dangerous stuff.

163
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:48,880
那你晚点得让我看看 好吗
You're gonna have to show me this later, okay?

164
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:49,700
没问题
Will do.

165
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,280
都怪你
Well, thanks to you,

166
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:54,200
我现在满身大汗 都没办法
now I'm all sweaty, and it's gonna be impossible

167
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:55,280
鉴定丝绸衬衫了
to judge the silk shirts.

168
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:56,980
应该宽松飘逸 而不是黏身上
They're supposed to blouse, not cling.

169
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:58,580
能让我看看这张卡吗
Hey, can I see that card for a second?

170
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:01,120
-你干什么 -等你把乔的头P到鳄鱼嘴里
- What are you doing? - I'll put this card back in your hand

171
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:03,580
我才会把这张卡交还给你
when you Photoshop that kid's head in an alligator's mouth.

172
00:06:04,775 --> 00:06:07,066
上游河谷在二码线上
Upper Valley on the 2-yard line

173
00:06:07,066 --> 00:06:08,660
比赛时间还剩十秒
with 10 seconds to go.

174
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:10,780
一个触地得分将会获胜
A touchdown will win the game.

175
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:12,335
暂停 暂停
Okay, timeout! Timeout!

176
00:06:12,483 --> 00:06:13,600
加油 海豚队
Let's go, Dolphins!

177
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:16,296
教练 我们怎么防守
Coach, what is our defense?

178
00:06:16,296 --> 00:06:18,000
好吧 按理说应该用奔跑达阵
Okay, you know what? It's a running situation,

179
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,640
但他们用传球虐我们一天了
but they've been killing us with that pass all day.

180
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:21,820
我的直觉认为他们要传球 但是...
My gut tells me they're gonna pass, but

181
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:22,740
好吧 让我想想
Okay, just let me think about it.

182
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:23,760
让开
Move. Move!

183
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:26,077
那些蠢货
Those dumb bastards

184
00:06:26,077 --> 00:06:29,538
肯定会认为我们要传球 所以我们要奔跑
are going to be thinking pass, which is why we're going to run.

185
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:30,800
左边用2包围防守
Trap Two, on the left side.

186
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:32,380
我的副校长对讲机
My vice principal walkie-talkie

187
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:34,080
不小心收听到了上游河谷教练
accidentally picked up that Upper Valley coach

188
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:35,320
说出她的白痴娘们战术
calling her dumb lady play.

189
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:37,678
我要改变我的防守策略吗
Now, was I gonna change my defense?

190
00:06:37,678 --> 00:06:41,620
只有没有骨气 全力争胜 追名逐利的人
Only some spineless win-at-all-costs glory hound

191
00:06:41,620 --> 00:06:44,740
才会选择赢 而不是展示高风亮节
would choose winning over showing some moral fiber.

192
00:06:44,996 --> 00:06:48,153
海豚队赢了 海豚队赢了
Dolphins win! Dolphins win!

193
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:54,482
体育场里的所有人 包括我
Everybody in that stadium, including me...

194
00:06:54,482 --> 00:06:55,640
-是啊 -都以为对方会传球
- Well... - was expecting a pass.

195
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:57,479
但你的直觉告诉你不会那样
But your instincts told you something else.

196
00:06:57,479 --> 00:06:58,739
真了不起 我的朋友
That's big-time, my friend.

197
00:06:58,739 --> 00:07:01,683
谢谢你这么说 杰 谢谢你
Well, I-I-I appreciate it, Jay. Uh, thank you.

198
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:02,200
米奇尔
Mitchell!

199
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:05,318
我是个骗子
I'm a fraud.

200
00:07:05,318 --> 00:07:06,831
那就别再和那个咖啡师吹牛
Well, then stop telling that barista

201
00:07:06,831 --> 00:07:08,782
说你在百老汇做过沙威[悲惨世界]的替角
that you understudied Javert on Broadway.

202
00:07:08,782 --> 00:07:10,700
他知道你叫什么 上网一查就发现了
He knows your name. He can look it up.

203
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:12,080
不 我不小心在对讲机上
No, I overheard the lady coach

204
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:13,360
听到那个女教练的战术安排
call her play on my walkie-talkie,

205
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,960
然后我改了我的防守策略赢了比赛
and I changed my defense to win the game.

206
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:17,299
现在我焦虑发作 我必须坦白
And now I'm having anxiety, and I have to confess.

207
00:07:17,299 --> 00:07:19,232
不行 你不能坦白
No, you-you are not gonna confess.

208
00:07:19,232 --> 00:07:21,300
你给我把焦虑揉成一个小球
You're gonna smush that anxiety into a little ball,

209
00:07:21,300 --> 00:07:23,080
再塞到你灵魂里那个专门用来
and you're gonna push it into that little, tiny hole

210
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:24,740
密封童年阴影的小洞里去
in your soul where childhood traumas go.

211
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:26,740
这里的所有人都是赢家
Everybody here is a winner.

212
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:29,080
如果最后你成了饭桌上唯一的失败者
I-If you end up being the one loser at the table,

213
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:32,200
我仅有的收获会是所有人居高临下的同情
I'm gonna get nothing but condescending pity from everybody.

214
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:34,598
特别是克莱尔那副难以忍受的虚伪嘴脸
Especially Claire, that insufferable phony.

215
00:07:34,598 --> 00:07:37,004
太漂亮了
Hey, so pretty!

216
00:07:40,908 --> 00:07:43,960
-卢克 -歌洛莉亚
- Luke. - Hey, Gloria.

217
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,240
你的刘海真好看
Sure love those bangs.

218
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:46,460
为什么剪了刘海
What's the story with those?

219
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:48,460
我知道你一直在躲着我
I know you have been avoiding me

220
00:07:48,460 --> 00:07:51,580
因为根本没有乔身处险境的合成照片
because there are no Photoshopped pictures of Joe in danger.

221
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,940
而你这个问题的答案很简单
And the the answer to your question is very simple --

222
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:54,920
刘海衬我的脸
They frame my face.

223
00:07:55,020 --> 00:07:56,360
那些照片啊
Oh, those pictures.

224
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:01,080
就在这
Here we are.

225
00:08:03,459 --> 00:08:05,768
乔捅蜂窝
Joe poking a bees' nest.

226
00:08:07,262 --> 00:08:10,580
乔射杀李·哈维·奥斯瓦尔德
Oh, and Joe killing Lee Harvey Oswald.

227
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:11,780
真可爱
So cute.

228
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:14,240
杰 卢克是个天才
Jay, Luke is a genius.

229
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:16,640
谢了 伙计
Thanks, buddy.

230
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:18,520
你可以去买高级衣服了
You can go do your fancy shopping now.

231
00:08:18,620 --> 00:08:20,420
太棒了 为了弥补我失去的时间
Awesome. To make up for the time I lost,

232
00:08:20,520 --> 00:08:21,640
我要给脚后跟涂上油
I'm gonna baby oil my heels

233
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:22,800
试鞋时穿脱就快多了
so I can try on shoes faster.

234
00:08:23,220 --> 00:08:26,300
菲尔 你看过卢克合成的这些照片了吗
Phil, did you see this Photoshop stuff that Luke did?

235
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,260
他真是个魔术师
He's a real magician.

236
00:08:27,260 --> 00:08:29,160
我想这是有其父必有其子
I guess he came by it honestly.

237
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:32,360
这话对我来说意义非凡 杰
That means the world to me, Jay.

238
00:08:32,660 --> 00:08:34,018
我的人生是场谎言
I'm living a lie.

239
00:08:34,018 --> 00:08:36,360
克莱尔 这家里的每个人都是赢家
Claire, everyone in this family's a winner

240
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:37,460
除了我
except for me.

241
00:08:37,460 --> 00:08:40,218
我变我变我变废柴
Abraka-failure.

242
00:08:40,380 --> 00:08:41,760
准备好灌水了吗
Ready to fill this thing up?

243
00:08:43,922 --> 00:08:45,120
我们之所以在这里拍
The-The whole reason we're here

244
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:47,180
就是为了用泳池水 能重复利用
is to use the pool water, which is recyclable.

245
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:49,640
我算是可持续魔术运动的大人物
I'm sort of a hero in the sustainable magic movement.

246
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:51,640
我可不想失去三只环保绿兔的评级
I'd hate to lose my three green rabbits rating.

247
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:52,740
好吧
Okay.

248
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,100
我们这就开拍吗
Should we start filming?

249
00:08:54,100 --> 00:08:56,139
当然 好 当然
For sure. Yeah. For sure.

250
00:08:56,139 --> 00:08:59,020
我认为我或许该先休息一下
I-I-I think I'll-I'll probably just take a quick minute.

251
00:08:59,020 --> 00:09:00,920
年轻时我表演什么魔术都不害怕
As a young man, I had no fear of any trick

252
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:02,420
任何被困在狭小空间的魔术都行
where I was jammed into tight spaces --

253
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:04,100
盒中狐 另一个牧羊人
Fox in a Box, The Wrong Shepherd,

254
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:05,400
爱因斯坦的鸟浴盆
Einstein's Birdbath.

255
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:09,100
不过最近 我多少有一点幽闭恐惧
Lately, though, I have had a touch of claustrophobia,

256
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:10,540
通常我只要
which is usually cleared up

257
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:12,980
给非常支持我的妻子打通电话就好了
by a quick call to my super-supportive wife.

258
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:14,820
你终于接电话了
Oh, you finally picked up.

259
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:16,480
不 没有紧急状况
No, no, it's not an emergency.

260
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:18,640
我只是...你在听吗 克莱尔
I just -- Hello? Claire?

261
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,080
等着你的指令呢 老爸
Just give me the word, Dad.

262
00:09:21,020 --> 00:09:21,420
好
Yep.

263
00:09:24,020 --> 00:09:24,580
我们
Let's...

264
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:26,516
-我们开始吧 -好 准备好了吗
- Let's do this. - Great. Ready?

265
00:09:26,516 --> 00:09:28,780
-好了 -开拍
- Yeah. - And...action.

266
00:09:28,780 --> 00:09:30,920
您好 恭喜您购买了这个
Hello, and congratulations on your purchase

267
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:32,020
诺曼底电话亭
of the Normandy Phone Booth.

268
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:33,520
接下来我将演示
The following will demonstrate

269
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:35,940
您为生活"拨动"了多少乐趣
just how much fun you've...dialed up.

270
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:44,640
今天就是登陆日
Here we are on D-Day.

271
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:46,080
该死的空中支援在哪
Where's the damned air support?

272
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:47,340
太好了
Oh, good.

273
00:09:49,185 --> 00:09:50,867
有个电话亭
A p-phone booth.

274
00:09:51,436 --> 00:09:53,760
我听说纳粹们在电话亭里设置了陷阱
I hear the Nazis have booby-trapped these,

275
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:54,600
但我...
but I will...

276
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:58,880
我绝对会以身犯险 给盟军司令部打电话
I definitely will take the risk of calling Allied Command.

277
00:10:04,380 --> 00:10:05,540
您好 上将
Hello, General.

278
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:09,680
是的 我们被敌人包围了
Yes, the enemy is all around us.

279
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,160
火力很猛
Blast!

280
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:16,340
这个电话亭里设置了陷阱
This is one of the phone booths that's booby-trapped.

281
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,720
不
Oh, no!

282
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:21,160
是的 上将 敌人正在逼近
Yes, General, the enemy is closing in!

283
00:10:21,894 --> 00:10:22,781
我们无路可逃...
There's no esca-

284
00:10:22,781 --> 00:10:24,326
海莉 快放我出去
Haley! Get me out of here!

285
00:10:24,326 --> 00:10:26,653
海莉是谁 我是卢瑟福护士
Who's Haley? I'm Nurse Rutherford.

286
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:28,980
如果我不能表演这个魔术
If I can't do this trick,

287
00:10:28,980 --> 00:10:32,155
我的魔术用品店会沦为小型商场的笑柄
my magic shop is gonna be the laughingstock of the mini-mall.

288
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:33,920
而那里还有一家过时多年的租片店呢
And there's still a Blockbuster there.

289
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:36,240
亲爱的 我知道你最近过得不顺
Honey, I know you're going through something,

290
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:37,620
但你不能告诉别人
but you need to keep it to yourself,

291
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:40,240
因为我们决不能成为今年家里的失败者
because we will not be the loser family this year.

292
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:41,680
-克莱尔 -怎么
- Claire. - Yeah?

293
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:42,748
我想到了一个天才点子
I had a genius idea.

294
00:10:42,748 --> 00:10:45,403
你的比赛路线正好经过普利切特衣橱
Your race went right by Pritchett's Closets.

295
00:10:45,413 --> 00:10:46,660
把保全摄像调出来
Pull the security tape.

296
00:10:46,660 --> 00:10:48,580
我们用你领先的画面冲副大广告
We'll blow up a frame of you in the lead and run a big ad --

297
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:51,520
"普利切特 三十年来一直领先于他人"
"Pritchett's. Leading the Pack for 30 Years."

298
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:53,720
-天才 -太赞了 老爸 真棒
- Genius! - I love it, Dad! Yes!

299
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:55,080
我这就去
I am on that!

300
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:57,300
我们有麻烦了
We have a problem.

301
00:10:57,820 --> 00:10:58,900
是我有麻烦了
I had a problem.

302
00:11:00,097 --> 00:11:02,062
你好
H-H-Hello?

303
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,880
你好 该死
Hello -- Damn it.

304
00:11:05,068 --> 00:11:06,580
菲尔 你最好是有紧急状况
Phil, this better be an emergency.

305
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:07,860
你终于接电话了
Oh, you finally picked up.

306
00:11:08,050 --> 00:11:09,720
不 没有紧急状况 我只是...
No, no, it's not an emergency. I just --

307
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:12,100
我在赛跑 歌单都因为你乱套了
I'm running a race, and you just screwed up my playlist!

308
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:19,000
从那一刻起
From that point on,

309
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:20,840
我就不在赛跑路线上了
I was no longer on the actual race course.

310
00:11:21,980 --> 00:11:22,860
谢谢你
Thank you!

311
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:26,380
谢谢
Thanks.

312
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:31,060
后来可能在某个转角我又兜回到比赛路线上
I guess I hit a point where I funneled back onto the course.

313
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:33,900
我的确注意到我的体能
I did notice that I seemed to have more energy

314
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:35,581
似乎比我前面的几个人充沛许多
than the few people in front of me,

315
00:11:35,581 --> 00:11:38,426
但我当时没多想
but I didn't-I didn't think much of it.

316
00:11:40,860 --> 00:11:43,140
我做到了 我赢了我赢了
I did it! I won! I won!

317
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:44,740
你看到了吗 宝贝 我赢了
Did you see that, honey? I won!

318
00:11:45,062 --> 00:11:46,120
不 你没赢
Uh, no, you didn't.

319
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:47,960
我一直站在五千米标志那 根本没看到你
I was standing at the 5K mark and never saw you.

320
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:49,660
-什么 -克莱尔
- What? - Claire!

321
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:52,500
我刚才在商店里 我看到你赢了
I was at the store, and I saw you win!

322
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:53,660
亲爱的
Oh, honey!

323
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:55,760
我认识她
I know her!

324
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:57,301
她是我继女
She's my stepdaughter!

325
00:11:57,301 --> 00:11:59,000
普利切特衣橱的保全摄像里
There's not gonna be any footage

326
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,240
根本不会有你跑过去的画面
of you running past Pritchett's Closets

327
00:12:00,240 --> 00:12:02,660
因为9.6公里的赛程你少跑了3公里
because you cut two miles out of a six-mile race.

328
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,260
你最好告诉外公你没赢
Better tell Grandpa you didn't win.

329
00:12:05,243 --> 00:12:07,220
你真是我的道德指南针
Oh, you are my moral compass.

330
00:12:07,220 --> 00:12:09,180
所以我今天一天都不想再和你说话了
Which is why I don't want to talk to you for the rest of the day.

331
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:10,060
卢克
Luke!

332
00:12:10,260 --> 00:12:12,020
帮我个忙 不许多问
I need a favor, no questions asked.

333
00:12:12,020 --> 00:12:13,300
你需要什么 匿名电话卡吗
What do you need? Phone cards?

334
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:16,180
不 我需要你合成一张
No. I need you to Photoshop a picture of me from today

335
00:12:16,180 --> 00:12:17,680
我今天跑过普利切特衣橱的照片
running in front of Pritchett's Closets.

336
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:20,020
没问题
No problem.

337
00:12:21,180 --> 00:12:25,200
-没问题 -我...
- No problem. - I --

338
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:26,600
我想拍张你和克莱尔的照片
I want to grab a picture of you and Claire.

339
00:12:26,780 --> 00:12:28,500
我想上传到内缝线账号上
I want to post it on my Inseam account.

340
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:29,420
内缝线是什么
Oh, what's Inseam?

341
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:30,860
我用来找自制成衣图样的软件
I use it for home tailoring.

342
00:12:31,060 --> 00:12:31,960
-克莱尔 -怎么
- Claire. - Yeah?

343
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:33,200
你能过来一下吗
Could you get in here, please?

344
00:12:33,420 --> 00:12:35,420
-我的两个超级明星 -好啊
- My two superstars. - Okay!

345
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:37,800
真不敢相信你膝盖不好还赢了比赛
Can't believe you won with that bad knee.

346
00:12:38,780 --> 00:12:41,240
还好 如果有人想偷奖牌的话
Well, at least if somebody tries to steal that thing,

347
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:42,400
他们得和这兄弟过过招
they got to get through this guy.

348
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:44,808
我不过是做了任何英雄会做的事
I just did what any hero would do.

349
00:12:44,808 --> 00:12:46,820
-没什么 -你化妆了吗
- It's... - Are you wearing makeup?

350
00:12:46,820 --> 00:12:48,319
是的 为了遮脸上的淤伤
Uh, well, yeah. I got a bruise.

351
00:12:48,319 --> 00:12:50,888
你不是说你一喊就把他吓跑了吗
I thought-I thought you screamed and he ran away?

352
00:12:50,888 --> 00:12:53,140
我们还是发生了肢体冲突的
Uh, well, there was a-there was a scuffle.

353
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:54,120
你听从了本能
You went with your instinct.

354
00:12:54,620 --> 00:12:56,040
反抗还是逃跑 你反抗了
Fight or flight. You fought.

355
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:58,160
我要把这张照片发到内缝线上
I'm gonna post this on Inseam.

356
00:12:58,540 --> 00:12:59,300
双击
Double-click.

357
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:00,460
该死的
Damn it.

358
00:13:01,060 --> 00:13:01,860
你反抗了
You fought.

359
00:13:02,760 --> 00:13:03,680
你反抗了
You fought?

360
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:05,380
你跟这个"闯空门的"多近距离接触了
How close did you get to this "intruder"?

361
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:07,620
克莱尔 你差不多够了
Okay, Claire. That is just about enough.

362
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:08,720
米奇尔遭受了创伤
Mitchell suffered a trauma,

363
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:11,060
我不喜欢你这种嘲讽的语气
and I don't appreciate your mocking tone.

364
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:12,580
容我们失陪 好吗
Excuse us. Okay?

365
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:14,800
谢谢你 亲爱的
Thank you, sweetie.

366
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:16,820
我们都能确定两件事
Okay, look, we both know two things for certain --

367
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,220
我穿珊瑚色特好看
I look fabulous in coral,

368
00:13:18,220 --> 00:13:20,110
你根本没打跑过任何闯空门的人
and you didn't fight off any intruder.

369
00:13:20,110 --> 00:13:21,800
这是有背景故事的
There-There is a backstory.

370
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:23,240
1984年夏天
In the summer of 1984,

371
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:24,740
在《小子难缠》的影响下
inspired by "The Karate Kid,"

372
00:13:24,820 --> 00:13:27,000
我那阵子特别沉迷于武术
I went through a martial arts phase.

373
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:29,060
当小卡把那副双节棍拿回家时
When Cam brought those nunchucks home,

374
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:30,960
我实在是无法抗拒
it was just too much to resist.

375
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:33,020
你好啊 老朋友
Hello, old friend.

376
00:13:34,432 --> 00:13:36,200
三十年后 又一次到了
30 years later, once again,

377
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:38,760
使出扫堂腿 技惊四座的时候了
it was time to sweep the leg.

378
00:13:46,306 --> 00:13:47,662
天啊 不
Oh, God. Oh, no!

379
00:13:55,480 --> 00:13:57,441
-你为什么不和我说实话 -我不知道
- Why didn't you just tell me? - I don't know.

380
00:13:57,441 --> 00:13:59,625
你进门就问我是不是有人闯进来了
You-You walked in, and you asked if there was a break-in,

381
00:13:59,625 --> 00:14:02,800
我当时很窘迫 还可能脑震荡了
and I-I was embarrassed and possibly concussed,

382
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,360
所以我就顺水推舟
so I just -- I went with it.

383
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:06,540
再说不能让我爸和克莱尔知道 明白吗
Besides, my dad and Claire cannot know, okay?

384
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:09,020
《小子难缠》上映的那年夏天 他们都叫我"功妇"
That whole "Karate Kid" summer, they called me "Kung Sue."

385
00:14:09,184 --> 00:14:13,803
火鸡10分钟后就好了
Turkey is gonna be ready in 10 minutes!

386
00:14:13,803 --> 00:14:16,140
-菲尔在哪 -我会告诉他
- Where is Phil? - I'll let him know.

387
00:14:16,140 --> 00:14:16,480
好
Okay.

388
00:14:18,644 --> 00:14:20,460
-再10分钟 -我做不来
- 10 minutes. - I can't take it!

389
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:21,440
你就深呼吸 老爸
Just breathe, Dad.

390
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:22,780
我们要克服你的恐惧
We are breaking this fear of yours.

391
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:23,720
我要死了
I'm dying here!

392
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:25,440
看着我
Look at me.

393
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:27,040
你想要你的余生
Do you want to spend the rest of your life

394
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:28,220
都只是一名开放空间魔术师吗
as an open-space magician?

395
00:14:30,860 --> 00:14:31,260
这就对了
Yeah.

396
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:37,300
杰 我在内缝线上看到乔的学校举办了
Jay, I saw on Inseam that there was a Thanksgiving pageant

397
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:38,320
感恩节大会
at Joe's school.

398
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:40,420
你为什么没告诉我
Why didn't you tell me?

399
00:14:41,620 --> 00:14:43,160
我忘了嘛
I totally forgot.

400
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:45,120
乔一周没上学了
Joe hasn't been in school for a week.

401
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:47,420
我跟他的老师起了点争执
I had a falling-out with his teacher.

402
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:49,988
然后被叫去校长办公室
And got sent to the principal's office.

403
00:14:49,988 --> 00:14:52,780
你对巴里什老师说了挺难听的话
You said some pretty harsh things to Mrs. Barrish.

404
00:14:52,780 --> 00:14:56,620
那是因为她在计划的餐会
In my defense, um, this banquet she's planning

405
00:14:56,620 --> 00:14:58,040
不符合史实
is not historically accurate.

406
00:14:58,660 --> 00:15:02,140
比如说 我不记得在首次感恩节餐会上
For example, I don't remember a tandoori chicken option

407
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:03,280
有印度咖喱鸡啊
at the first Thanksgiving.

408
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:05,620
我们学校有不同文化种族的孩子
We have children here from many ethnicities,

409
00:15:05,620 --> 00:15:07,340
我们想让大家都有参与感
and we try to make them all feel included.

410
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:11,560
尽管如此 史书上也没写过餐会时 印第安人
Be that as it may, history does not record Pocahontas

411
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:14,900
请英国探险家帮忙递生鱼片寿司卷
asking John Smith to pass the sashimi roll

412
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:16,994
而英国知名军官也在一旁
while Myles Standish helps himself

413
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:19,340
给自己来点无麸质墨西哥煎蛋
to gluten-free huevos rancheros!

414
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:22,720
之后火气越来越大 我们被逐出学校
After that, it got heated, and we got expelled.

415
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:23,640
"我们"吗
"We"?

416
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:26,100
他们会打来的
But they'll call.

417
00:15:26,340 --> 00:15:27,240
始终需要我的银子
They need my check.

418
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:29,441
为什么学校什么都没告诉我
Why didn't the school tell me anything?

419
00:15:29,441 --> 00:15:31,863
好像我不在电邮通知名单上了
It's like I am off their e-mail list.

420
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:34,580
我都没看到过他的变装服
I didn't even see the costumes.

421
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:36,240
他不用变装啊
Well, he didn't have a costume.

422
00:15:36,460 --> 00:15:38,860
他是解说员 他负责说出整个故事
No, he was the narrator. Kid told the whole story.

423
00:15:38,959 --> 00:15:40,513
小乖乖
Ay, papi.

424
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:43,220
你当时一定超可爱
You must have been so cute.

425
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:45,898
晚餐的时候给大家表演一次吧
Why don't you perform it for everybody at dinner?

426
00:15:45,898 --> 00:15:48,595
我去拿我的手机 我们得录下来
I'll go get my phone, and we'll film it.

427
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:50,300
-好吗 -没问题
- Okay? - Yes.

428
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:54,340
小家伙 我得最快时间帮你补课
I gotta get you up to speed in a hurry, buddy.

429
00:15:55,780 --> 00:15:58,920
感恩节的故事 开始
The story of Thanksgiving. Here goes.

430
00:15:58,920 --> 00:15:59,120
没用
It's no use!

431
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:01,540
我做不到
I can't do it!

432
00:16:10,228 --> 00:16:12,183
我了个去 她成功了
Sonuvabitch, she did it!

433
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:14,320
你们看到了吗
See that, people?

434
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:16,600
又一个超越自己巅峰的人 都感谢我
Another person doing their best, thanks to me.

435
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:18,520
现在可以开吃了
It's time to eat.

436
00:16:18,960 --> 00:16:19,660
谷歌
Hey, Google,

437
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:22,080
火鸡还要多久
how much time left on the turkey?

438
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:22,855
两分钟
Two minutes.

439
00:16:22,855 --> 00:16:25,960
看到没 我能控制那个神经病甜甜圈
See? I can control that crazy doughnut,

440
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:26,920
也成功达到十万步
I can do the steps.

441
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,460
我做到了两件事
I have two achievements,

442
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:30,040
而其他人只做到了一件
and the rest have only one.

443
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:31,480
所以外公真的靠
So, Grandpa really motivated you

444
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:32,900
说你做不到什么而激励了你是吧
by telling you you couldn't do something, huh?

445
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:35,160
我要看看这个计步器 我写报告要用
I need to see that My StepCounter for a paper I'm writing.

446
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:38,520
大家都成功做到了一些事
Everybody achieved something today,

447
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:40,460
现在轮到乔了
so now it's Joe's turn.

448
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:41,220
乔
Joe...

449
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:44,035
跟我们说说第一个感恩节的故事
tell us about the first Thanksgiving.

450
00:16:44,035 --> 00:16:45,340
来吧 小家伙
Come up here, buddy.

451
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:46,440
你能行
You got this.

452
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:50,260
曾有一片大地住着不信神的原住民
There was once a land of godless natives.

453
00:16:50,460 --> 00:16:51,980
他们愚蠢无知
They did not know any better

454
00:16:51,980 --> 00:16:54,060
直到某天 白人们来了
until, one day, the white man arrived.

455
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:55,498
这是什么鬼
What is this?

456
00:16:55,498 --> 00:16:57,994
白人们可怜这些原始人
The white man took pity on these primitives

457
00:16:57,994 --> 00:17:00,840
教导他们如何耕种土地
by teaching them to cultivate the land.

458
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:03,980
但他们的善良被误会为侵略
But their kindness was mistaken for aggression,

459
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:06,160
所以战争开打了
and a war began.

460
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:08,640
这是哪门子的鬼学校
What kind of school is this?

461
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:10,480
-我小时候学到的也是这样 -什么
- This is what I was taught. - What?

462
00:17:11,460 --> 00:17:14,180
最后 一切回归和平
Eventually, peace was restored,

463
00:17:14,180 --> 00:17:18,100
我们还送给了他们我国最高荣誉
and we bestowed them with our nation's highest honor --

464
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:20,040
让他们冠名橄榄球队
naming football teams for them.

465
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:22,021
乔 这是什么短剧
Joe, what play is this?

466
00:17:22,021 --> 00:17:25,090
我没有演出短剧 我都没上学了
I wasn't in a play! I don't go to school anymore!

467
00:17:28,480 --> 00:17:29,500
好啦 对啦
All right, fine.

468
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:31,420
我们被踢出来了可以吗
We got kicked out, okay?

469
00:17:31,620 --> 00:17:33,060
跟校长小小吵了一架
Little argument with the principal.

470
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:34,620
你怎么可以骗我
You've been lying to me

471
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:38,320
亏我还一直夸你是个超棒的父亲
while I was celebrating you as an amazing father?

472
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:39,856
歌洛莉亚 奇怪了
Hey, Gloria, this is weird.

473
00:17:39,856 --> 00:17:42,380
我下载了你的计步器数据
You know, I downloaded your My StepCounter data

474
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:43,177
到我电脑里
onto my computer,

475
00:17:43,177 --> 00:17:44,920
数据显示你今早走的路线
and it's showing your path this morning

476
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:46,520
跟我妈妈去赛跑的路线是一样的
was the same route my mom took in her race.

477
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:51,060
我怎么可能跑得到十万步
I was never going to get 100,000 steps.

478
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:54,300
一直到后来我知道克莱尔要去火鸡赛跑
But then I learned that Claire was going on a Turkey Trot.

479
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:56,080
第二次我抱她时
The second time I hugged her,

480
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:58,219
比第一次不容易 因为她浑身是汗
it was a little harder because she was really wet.

481
00:17:58,219 --> 00:18:01,580
所以我基本上就是你的计步代跑骡吗
So I'm basically just your StepCounter mule?

482
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:03,020
我还以为你在乎我这场跑步呢
I thought you cared about my race.

483
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:04,520
我很爱你 克莱尔
I love you very much, Claire,

484
00:18:04,520 --> 00:18:07,480
但我对你的运动真的没兴趣
but your exercise doesn't really interest me.

485
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:10,561
等等 克莱尔什么时候经过公司的来着
Hang on. When did Claire run past Pritchett's Closets?

486
00:18:10,561 --> 00:18:12,995
因为上面显示她压根就没靠近过那里
'Cause this thing says she never got near it.

487
00:18:12,995 --> 00:18:15,295
爸 估计是计步器出错了
Well, it's probably the StepCounter made a mistake.

488
00:18:15,295 --> 00:18:16,880
是吗 还是...
Oh, yeah, did it? Or -- Or --

489
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:18,480
还是你绕捷径了
Or did you take a little shortcut?

490
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:20,019
才没有 应该是我跑太快
No, I was probably going so fast

491
00:18:20,019 --> 00:18:21,327
它都跟不上我的脚步
it couldn't even keep up with me.

492
00:18:21,327 --> 00:18:23,480
-我有照片为证 -让我看...
- I have a picture of it. - Let me see.

493
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:24,020
卢克
Luke?

494
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:26,560
你们看
And there you go.

495
00:18:26,700 --> 00:18:29,299
很清楚能看到我跑过普里契特衣柜公司
That is me clearly running in front of Pritchett's Closets.

496
00:18:29,299 --> 00:18:31,620
对啊 窗上还有
Oh, yeah, yeah. With a Reagan/Bush poster

497
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:32,920
84年总统大选的海报呢
in the window, huh?

498
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:34,460
照片是假的
The photo is a fake.

499
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:36,760
不能怪我 是曼尼改的图
It's not my fault. Manny made it.

500
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:38,560
曼尼改了所有的图吗
Manny was photoshopping everything?

501
00:18:38,940 --> 00:18:40,768
所以乔真的发生危险了吗
So Joe was in real danger?

502
00:18:40,768 --> 00:18:42,780
我没想到你这么轻易
I did not realize how easy it would be

503
00:18:42,780 --> 00:18:43,856
就能把线索都连上
for you to connect those dots.

504
00:18:43,856 --> 00:18:45,420
对你挺失望的 卢克
Pretty disappointed in you, Luke.

505
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:47,520
他从哪学坏的 我想大家都懂
Well, you know, it's easy to see where he learned it from.

506
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:48,896
他老妈就是个骗子
His mother's a cheater!

507
00:18:48,896 --> 00:18:52,130
什么 你少跟我搞这套义愤填膺的了
What?! Oh, don't get so hot and bothered. Uh-huh! Mm.

508
00:18:52,130 --> 00:18:53,640
-你的妆都要花了 你这... -别碰我
- Your makeup's already running, and what do... - Stop it.

509
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:55,779
你的淤青上有个中文字吗
Do you have a Chinese character on your bruise?

510
00:18:55,779 --> 00:18:57,883
估计是闯入的人打我时 他戒指的字印的
Yeah, it's probably an imprint from the intruder's ring.

511
00:18:57,883 --> 00:19:00,380
他... 我确定他肯定是混什么帮派之类的
He was -- I'm sure he was in a gang of some sort.

512
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:01,360
老实交代吧 米奇尔
Just give it up, Mitchell.

513
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:02,980
他玩我以代理副校长职权
He knocked himself out with some nunchucks

514
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:04,858
没收的双节棍时不小心打到了自己
that I confiscated as acting vice principal.

515
00:19:04,858 --> 00:19:07,420
天啊 功妇又回来了
Oh, my God! Kung Sue is back.

516
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:08,237
老爸 你听到了吗
Daddy, did you hear that?

517
00:19:08,237 --> 00:19:11,989
小卡 小卡不是靠实力赢的球赛
Well, Cam -- Cam didn't really win the football game.

518
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,518
他从对方女教练那里偷听人家战术
Uh-huh. He stole the last play from the lady coach!

519
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:16,220
是意外 我不小心在我做为代理副校长
Accidentally! I overheard it on a walkie-talkie

520
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:18,820
必需要有的对讲机里听到的
that I require as an acting vice principal,

521
00:19:19,060 --> 00:19:20,820
我对这职位感到十分骄傲
which is a position I'm pretty proud of

522
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:21,880
因为我基本就是个警长
because I'm basically a sheriff.

523
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:24,520
-你才不... -就是 我基本就是警长
- You're not basically -- No. Yes, I am basically a sheriff!

524
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:26,040
我戴着帽子
I wear a hat!

525
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:30,600
爸要表演那个魔术了 他从来没做过呢
Dad is doing his trick, and he's never done it before.

526
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:31,240
有可能会死
He could die.

527
00:19:32,710 --> 00:19:33,587
快来
Come on!

528
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:35,760
菲尔 亲爱的 别啊
Oh, Phil. Honey, wait!

529
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:37,560
-你不用做这个的 -我必须要做
- You don't have to do this. - Yes, I do!

530
00:19:38,020 --> 00:19:41,260
我是一大家人生赢家里的唯一废柴
I'm the only loser in a remarkable family of winners.

531
00:19:41,360 --> 00:19:42,580
不不 不是的
No, no, no!

532
00:19:42,580 --> 00:19:43,980
我们才不是什么赢家
We are not all winners!

533
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:46,560
其实我们全都是废柴
It turned out we all stink!

534
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:47,860
无所谓了
It doesn't matter!

535
00:19:47,960 --> 00:19:49,980
不想要被恐惧支配我的人生
I don't want to live a life ruled by fear!

536
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:52,240
我今天就得表演这个魔术
I have to do this trick today.

537
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:55,140
不过有点越来越难呼吸了
Although, it is getting hard to breathe!

538
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:56,960
别停 老爸 你可以的
Don't stop, Dad! You can do this!

539
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:57,898
我对你有信心
I believe in you!

540
00:19:57,898 --> 00:20:00,240
-这话说了没用啊 宝贝 -有意思
- That's not helping, honey! - Very interesting.

541
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:01,849
我一鼓作气做完吧
Okay, I'm just gonna try to barrel through this.

542
00:20:01,849 --> 00:20:05,000
这里是诺曼底 我是美国大兵托尼·兰切提
It's Normandy. I'm an American G.I. Named Tony Ranzetti.

543
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,180
我来自布鲁克林 我最爱我妈做的家常菜
I'm from Brooklyn, and I love my mama's home cooking!

544
00:20:07,180 --> 00:20:08,679
但我觉得我逃不出来了
But I don't think I'm gonna be able to get out!

545
00:20:08,679 --> 00:20:11,600
是托尼的台词 还是菲尔真逃不出
Is he talking as Tony Ranzetti or as Phil?

546
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:12,980
你们这些孬种有病啊
What is wrong with you cowards?!

547
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,320
菲尔需要帮忙
Phil needs help!

548
00:20:14,990 --> 00:20:16,859
功妇再次出击
Kung Sue's back at it.

549
00:20:20,434 --> 00:20:21,896
来不及逃啦
It's too late to get out! Oh.

550
00:20:21,896 --> 00:20:24,120
-不要啊 -这就是个错误
-No! -This was a mistake!!

551
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:25,420
好像真的不对 老爸
Something's wrong. Dad?

552
00:20:25,580 --> 00:20:26,780
天啊 菲尔 菲尔
Oh, God. Phil! Phil!

553
00:20:29,604 --> 00:20:32,983
-天啊 -什 什么...
- Oh, my God! -What -- What...

554
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:35,020
哇靠 他上哪去了
Holy crap, where'd he go?!

555
00:20:35,020 --> 00:20:39,720
兰切提二等兵报告 天神作战成功
Private Ranzetti reporting Operation Overlord is a success.

556
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:42,480
鸡尾酒我请
Cocktails are on me.

557
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:45,060
太厉害了 谁都不服就服你 菲尔
That was amazing! Gotta hand it to you, Phil.

558
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:46,580
火鸡的大鸡腿给你吃
You get the big turkey leg.

559
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:48,480
派对重新回到桌上
Let's take this party to the table!

560
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:51,120
不赞吗 嬉皮士们
Come on, hippies.

561
00:20:55,020 --> 00:20:56,600
小卡 很晚了
Cam. It's late.

562
00:20:58,820 --> 00:21:01,440
小卡 我明天得早起干活
Cam, I have work early in the morning.

563
00:21:04,060 --> 00:21:06,220
卡梅隆 你这样我没法睡
Cameron! I cannot sleep!

564
00:21:06,500 --> 00:21:07,620
那你下次应该先考虑清楚
Well, you should have thought about that

565
00:21:07,620 --> 00:21:09,330
再挑衅我 发出我无法在一天内
before you challenged me that I couldn't do

566
00:21:09,330 --> 00:21:10,739
跑完十万步的挑战啊
100,000 steps in a day.

567
00:21:10,739 --> 00:21:12,118
你还差多少
Well, how close are you?

568
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:14,242
好吧 行
Okay, fine.

569
00:21:16,840 --> 00:21:18,580
等等 是剩125步吧
Wait. 125 left?

570
00:21:18,780 --> 00:21:19,189
不是
Nope.

571
00:21:19,189 --> 00:21:20,260
天啊
Oh, my God.
